  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1241 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nWednesday will begin in a slightly cooler post-frontal air mass, \nwith high temperatures 5-10 degrees cooler than the previous day, \nmainly low to mid-80s for the Nebraska Panhandle and mid-70s \nelsewhere. The ridge continues to elongate through the middle of the \nwork week, placing our area in primarily zonal flow aloft and \ntherefore mostly dry conditions. A warming trend is expected on \nThursday and Friday as a secondary ridge begins to build across the \nDesert Southwest. Will have to monitor fire weather conditions on \nboth of these days as ensemble guidance is hinting at gusty westerly \nwinds of 25-35 knots combined with daytime RH values dipping to 15-\n20%. \n\nHeading into the weekend, we start to bring back the fetch of \nmonsoonal moisture ahead of a shortwave trough digging across the \nPacific Northwest, placing Southeastern Wyoming and Western Nebraska \nin WSW flow aloft. With the lack of signal for any substantial \nforcing from long-range ensemble guidance, no widespread (and \nbeneficial) precipitation is expected. However can expect a slight \ncooling trend with this next push of moisture and the usual diurnal \npattern of scattered afternoon and evening showers and\nthunderstorms.",
